==English==

===Etymology===
From ''[[I]]'', ''[[don't]]'' and ''[[think]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/aɪ dəʊnt θɪŋk/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/aː doʊnt θɪŋk/}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{non-gloss definition|used after a [[statement]] to indicate an [[emphatic]] or [[ironic]] [[negative]]}}
#: ''There are lots of good things to watch on the telly tonight - '''I don't think'''!''

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bender}}, {{l|en|not}}

